I have played the game many times. I always spend about a week, maybe two doing everything I can in regards to side quests and the campaign. I always give up after a certain amount of time because the game doesn't hold my interest for long enough.

&nbsp;

I loathe card games. There is nothing fun to me about games like that.

&nbsp;

I loved playing that mini-game. Shit got *intense*. Battling people from the protagonist's past just to gain more cards for all of my decks. Battling kids in random villages that are experts for the very same reason. Travelling all across the map just to complete related quests.

&nbsp;

In some regard, that mini-game was the only thing bringing me back to the game.

A major dictionary is your friend here pal, sorry to say that you are *wrong*. Stupider is a comparative form of "stupid".



"We list *stupider* and *stupidest* as the comparative and superlative forms of *stupid*, because that is what they are. They are honest-to-goodness, one-hundred-percent, grade-A, real words. In case anyone tries to tell you otherwise here is a small sample of them being used in edited prose over the ages:"

&amp;#x200B;

&gt;…part and counterpart wandered independently about the earth in the  stupidest  manner for a while, till the late time came.  
— a famous author, *a classic novel*, 1891  
&gt;  
&gt;  
"All ladies like them, I suppose," said that  stupidest  and most stubborn of all humble friends, a female character.  
— another famous author, *another classic novel*, 1873  
&gt;  
&gt;  
Death, insanity/suicide degeneration  
that is, just getting  stupider  as they get older  
— a famous poet, *a famous poem collection*, 1972  
&gt;  
&gt;  
A character suspects, as does the neighborhood woman who gives the film a piquant fairy-tale quality when her dog is stolen in the opening scene, that for some reason people are getting stupider and stupider all the time.  
— a film critic, *a major newspaper*, 27 Feb. 1998

Here [is the link to the above examples.](https://www.merriam-webster.com/words-at-play/are-stupider-and-stupidest-real-words)
